 "review": {
  "score": 5.0,
  "round": 1,
  "problems": [
   "The silhouette is a closed, pointed egg (widest at y\u2248-184, narrowing to a point at the base and rounding at the top). At a glance it reads as a balloon, a lantern or a pink tree in a glass dome. It does not read as a gorgonian fan, which flares wide and flat toward the top from a short stalk.",
   "Five evenly spaced horizontal arcs (y -90, -135, -178, -218, -246) cross a thick central spine (lw 6). Together they read as a rib cage, a fish skeleton or a globe with meridians, not an organic lattice.",
   "The lattice is too sparse and too regular. There are only 4 thin diagonal lines, so the fine-mesh 'lace' quality of a sea fan is missing.",
   "The pink and champagne bead tips on the branch ends look like fairy lights or ornaments. That makes it read even more like a decorated tree.",
   "The base and holdfast (charcoal rock at y 0 to -22, gold cap at y -28) almost vanish next to the person. The fan looks like it is balanced on a pin rather than rooted.",
   "The envelope fill at a=0.28 looks muddy, and the edge has no organic, scalloped outline."
  ]
 },
 "for": "Tall, flat, lattice-like gorgonian sea fan in rose or violet, swaying gently in the current. It gives the reef vertical layers for the dolphins to weave between",
 "source": "minted",
 "created": "2026-11-02"
}